1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,507
Web3 has a compliance paradox.

2
00:00:03,327 --> 00:00:11,150
Traditional KYC stores passports, faces, and addresses in centralized databases.

3
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:14,861
Fully anonymous DeFi gets shut down by regulators.

4
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:20,525
Until now, users had to choose: expose their privacy, or break the law.

5
00:00:21,668 --> 00:00:24,467
And compliance never stops changing.

6
00:00:24,287 --> 00:00:32,110
When a wallet hits a sanctions list, access may stay open for days because revocation depends on manual updates.

7
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:36,667
One centralized failure point, for users and protocols alike.

8
00:00:37,796 --> 00:00:40,712
ZK-CID fixes both sides.

9
00:00:40,532 --> 00:00:49,019
We combine decentralized identity with zero-knowledge proofs, so a user can prove I am compliant without revealing who I am.

10
00:00:48,839 --> 00:00:55,178
The issuer verifies documents off-chain and stores only an anonymous commitment.

11
00:00:54,998 --> 00:00:59,801
The protocol sees a valid proof, never the person's identity.

12
00:01:00,956 --> 00:01:02,466
Let us see it live.

13
00:01:04,456 --> 00:01:05,549
Step one.

14
00:01:05,369 --> 00:01:10,354
The user generates a Semaphore identity locally in the browser.

15
00:01:10,174 --> 00:01:13,244
The private key never leaves the device.

16
00:01:14,456 --> 00:01:15,601
Step two.

17
00:01:15,421 --> 00:01:19,911
A trusted issuer verifies the user's documents off-chain.

18
00:01:19,731 --> 00:01:24,729
Only the anonymous commitment is added to the on-chain compliance group.

19
00:01:25,856 --> 00:01:27,170
Step three.

20
00:01:26,990 --> 00:01:33,707
To enter a regulated DeFi app, the user generates a zero-knowledge proof in the browser.

21
00:01:33,527 --> 00:01:37,118
It proves approved-group membership and prevents replay.

22
00:01:36,938 --> 00:01:41,637
ComplianceGate verifies it and mints the Access NFT.

23
00:01:42,856 --> 00:01:44,066
Step four.

24
00:01:43,886 --> 00:01:52,308
When a sanctions list changes, the Chainlink CRE workflow matches on-chain members and revokes the credential automatically.

25
00:01:52,128 --> 00:01:54,626
No manual update, no delay.

26
00:01:55,768 --> 00:02:07,369
Under the hood: Semaphore v4 for anonymous membership, Solidity and Hardhat for on-chain verification, and a Next.js frontend on Scaffold-ETH 2.

27
00:02:07,189 --> 00:02:12,213
Chainlink CRE orchestrates the complete compliance lifecycle.

28
00:02:13,336 --> 00:02:14,872
This is not a mock-up.

29
00:02:14,692 --> 00:02:20,419
Contracts are deployed on Sepolia, and the end-to-end flow is covered by tests.

30
00:02:20,239 --> 00:02:26,109
The CRE simulation executes fetch, match, report, and revoke.

31
00:02:25,929 --> 00:02:31,747
Any DeFi protocol can integrate the gate without taking custody of user data.

32
00:02:31,567 --> 00:02:34,755
Regulators get verifiable compliance.

33
00:02:34,575 --> 00:02:36,669
Users keep their privacy.

34
00:02:37,816 --> 00:02:42,060
The live demo and open-source code are ready for judges to test.

35
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:46,370
ZK-CID: private by design, compliant by proof.

36
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:47,242
Thank you.
